    "updated_at": "2025-12-03T16:39:14Z",
    "body": "The lack of WPTs, at least, was due to some uncertainty over what exactly a \"fixed\" spec would look like. While the addition of [#inform-the-navigation-api-about-aborting-navigation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#inform-the-navigation-api-about-aborting-navigation) for download navigations was expected, this doesn't really address the issue that *successful* downloads never result in the ongoing navigate event being cleared. So while adding the abort does mean that the assertion no longer fails, it still means that firing multiple successful downloads in a row will cause `navigateerror`s to occur, despite there having been no actual errors.",
